{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"title","type":"text","x":0,"y":-420,"width":2380,"height":170,"color":"5","text":"# Saved reels pipeline: how it works, step by step (built 2026-10-08)\nRead left to right, then the second row. **Green** = built and proven today. **Yellow** = decided or partly built. **Red** = secret. **Purple** = what you learn at that step.\nGoal: every reel you save on Instagram gets downloaded, fully analysed, turned into a list of actions, audited, and filed in Obsidian. Nothing is missed, nothing is installed unless it is safe."},
		{"id":"s0","type":"text","x":0,"y":0,"width":420,"height":300,"color":"4","text":"## 0. Your Saved collections\nInstagram > profile > Saved. Folders so far: **AI cooking** (127 reels), **test reels** (4), plus website finishing, filming, sales, backend, fashion, coding, life maxxing, powerlifting, looks.\nYou choose which folders count. A reel can sit in several folders."},
		{"id":"s1","type":"text","x":480,"y":0,"width":420,"height":300,"color":"4","text":"## 1. Collect the links\n`collect_links.py \"AI cooking\"`\nPlaywright opens a real Chrome window with your session cookies, clicks the folder, scrolls slowly and reads every reel link off the page. Read only. Stops at once on a login or challenge page.\nFile: `C:\\dev\\reels\\collector\\collect_links.py`"},
		{"id":"s2","type":"text","x":960,"y":0,"width":420,"height":300,"color":"4","text":"## 2. Ledger + queue\n`ledger.csv` has one row per reel: id, link, folder, status (queued > downloaded > analysed > actioned, or failed), time.\n`queue/links.txt` holds links not yet sent. A reel already known or already downloaded is never queued twice.\nFolder: `C:\\dev\\reels\\`"},
		{"id":"s3","type":"text","x":1440,"y":0,"width":420,"height":300,"color":"4","text":"## 3. Send to the bot\nThe links are typed into your Telegram chat with **Reel Saver** (`@yusha_reel_saver_bot`), using screen control (Windows-MCP). All 4 test links took seconds to type.\nTelegram holds them in order. The bot takes one at a time, **30 s apart**, pauses 10 min on a 429, stops on a login challenge."},
		{"id":"s4","type":"text","x":1920,"y":0,"width":420,"height":300,"color":"4","text":"## 4. Download\n`reel_bot.py` runs **yt-dlp** with your cookies and saves `ig_<id>.mp4` + `ig_<id>.info.json` (caption, creator, likes) into `C:\\dev\\reels\\1-inbox`.\nProven: 6 reels, 6 for 6, about 7 s each.\nReplies in Telegram: \"Saved: name, length, size\" or \"Already saved\"."},
		{"id":"l0","type":"text","x":0,"y":340,"width":420,"height":220,"color":"6","text":"**You learn: the source of truth**\nInstagram's page is the only list of what you saved. Instagram redirects direct folder URLs to the main Saved page, so the script has to *click* the folder like a person. Always count what you really got: my first count was 12, the real number was **127** (the page loads in chunks, I scrolled too fast)."},
		{"id":"l1","type":"text","x":480,"y":340,"width":420,"height":220,"color":"6","text":"**You learn: polite automation**\nOne slow browser, random 2-4 s pauses, no proxies, no tricks. It uses your real session, so a block would hit your account. The script stops at the first sign of a login or challenge instead of retrying."},
		{"id":"l2","type":"text","x":960,"y":340,"width":420,"height":220,"color":"6","text":"**You learn: a ledger makes it safe to rerun**\nBecause every reel has a status, you can run the collector every day and only new reels get queued. Same idea as a database primary key. Bug found: PowerShell added a hidden byte-order mark to the CSV, so Python must read it as `utf-8-sig`."},
		{"id":"l3","type":"text","x":1440,"y":340,"width":420,"height":220,"color":"6","text":"**You learn: queues and pacing**\nYou do not wait 30 s between sending. Telegram is the queue, the bot is the slow worker. Sending is fast, downloading is rate-limited on purpose. Gate 2 proof: 4 links typed back to back, saved at 7:22:44, 7:23:19, 7:23:55, 7:24:30."},
		{"id":"l4","type":"text","x":1920,"y":340,"width":420,"height":220,"color":"6","text":"**You learn: why cookies are secret**\n`cookies.txt` = your logged-in Instagram. Anyone holding it can act as you. It lives only in `C:\\dev\\reels\\`, never in chat, notes or git. The bot token (`.telegram-token`) is the same kind of secret."},
		{"id":"s5","type":"text","x":0,"y":680,"width":420,"height":380,"color":"4","text":"## 5. Analyse, part A (local, no Claude)\n`analyze_reel.py` (per reel, 36-45 s on your RTX 3060):\n- audio out (ffmpeg)\n- **Whisper** words with timestamps, language\n- 1 frame per second + an extra frame 0.2 s after every scene cut\n- scene cuts (scenedetect)\n- caption, creator, title from the `.info.json`\n- **coverage report**: seconds with speech, language, flags (music only, odd language, missed frame)\nOutput: `C:\\dev\\reels\\3-analysed\\ig_<id>\\timeline.md`"},
		{"id":"s6","type":"text","x":480,"y":680,"width":420,"height":380,"color":"3","text":"## 6. Analyse, part B (Claude)\nI read caption + transcript (+ frames where text shows on screen) and write the **actions**: a skill to get, a tool to try, a tip to follow.\nAbout 10 reels per pass, one record per reel, about 1-3K tokens each.\nGated posts (\"comment X for the link\") are never answered from your account without asking you; I find the likely source by web search instead and mark it unverified.\nNot yet automated: you say \"analyze today's\"."},
		{"id":"s7","type":"text","x":960,"y":680,"width":420,"height":380,"color":"3","text":"## 7. Act: audit, then install or ask\n1. Find the real source (web search)\n2. Clone to **quarantine** `C:\\dev\\reels\\quarantine\\` (nothing runs)\n3. Audit: read the files, no unknown hosts, no obfuscation, no secrets access, no install scripts that run downloaded code, source looks real\n4. **Safe** -> install. **Doubtful** -> do not install, report and ask you.\n5. Check overlap with what you already have.\nDone for 5 reels: nothing needed installing yet."},
		{"id":"s8","type":"text","x":1440,"y":680,"width":420,"height":380,"color":"3","text":"## 8. File it + clean up\nEvery skill or tool gets a note in `Resources/reel-skills/` (what, source, reel, audit, overlap, status, undo). Installed ones also go in `skills-list` and `tools-in-use`.\nActions per reel are in `reel-actions.md`.\n**Delete rule:** the downloaded video is deleted about 7 days after its actions are extracted. Transcript, frames, notes and the ledger row stay. **Nothing is ever deleted from Instagram.**"},
		{"id":"l5","type":"text","x":0,"y":1100,"width":420,"height":240,"color":"6","text":"**You learn: why local first**\nAudio, frames, words and cuts cost no Claude usage, so they run on your PC. Claude is used only where judgement is needed. GPU note: Whisper needed two NVIDIA libraries (cuBLAS, cuDNN) installed with pip, not the 3 GB CUDA Toolkit."},
		{"id":"l6","type":"text","x":480,"y":1100,"width":420,"height":240,"color":"6","text":"**You learn: do not miss anything**\nVoice alone misses things. In one reel the caption held the full list of 5 skills while the voiceover only half said it. Hence caption + frames + coverage flags, and the video is kept 7 days so any miss can be redone."},
		{"id":"l7","type":"text","x":960,"y":1100,"width":420,"height":240,"color":"6","text":"**You learn: untrusted code**\nReels sell links, not safety. Example: the Ootto repo was clean except one skill that tells the agent to install unknown tools and take cookies. Hooks (code that runs on every action) are the highest-risk part of any skill pack, so they get read first."},
		{"id":"l8","type":"text","x":1440,"y":1100,"width":420,"height":240,"color":"6","text":"**You learn: write it down once**\nA registry note per skill saves rediscovering the same repo later. Each note answers: what is it, which reel, is it safe, do I already have it, how do I undo it."},
		{"id":"nums","type":"text","x":1920,"y":680,"width":420,"height":380,"color":"5","text":"## Real numbers so far (2026-10-08)\n- Collections read: 2 (AI cooking 127, test reels 4)\n- Downloaded + analysed: **5 reels**\n- Still queued: **122**\n- Bot: 6 for 6 downloads, no 429, no challenge\n- Analysis: 36-45 s per reel (GPU), no coverage flags\n- Estimate for the 122: about 70 min to download (35 s each), about 80 min to analyse\n- Repos audited: 3 (Ootto, Everything Claude Code, Open Design). Installed: 0"},
		{"id":"todo","type":"text","x":1920,"y":1100,"width":420,"height":240,"color":"3","text":"## Not built yet\n- Hourly automatic loop (you said not yet)\n- Auto-run of analysis after each download\n- Frame text reading by a local vision model (untested)\n- The 7-day video delete script\n- A bot that comments for gated links (later, your call)\n- Gate 3: 25 real links; gate 4: the rest, max 100 a day"},
		{"id":"lessons","type":"text","x":0,"y":1400,"width":2380,"height":230,"color":"1","text":"## Things that broke while building (and why) - good to remember\n1. **Taskbar icons shift**, so clicking them opened the wrong app twice. Fix: switch windows by name, check the screen before typing.\n2. **My count of 12 reels was wrong (127)**: scrolling faster than the page loads. Fix: scroll slowly until nothing new appears 3 times.\n3. **GPU Whisper crashed** on a missing library (`cublas64_12.dll`). Fix: `pip install nvidia-cublas-cu12 nvidia-cudnn-cu12`, point the script at the folders.\n4. **A scene cut at the very end of a video has no frame after it.** Fix: step back and retry, flag it if still missing.\n5. **CSV with a hidden BOM** (PowerShell Export-Csv) made Python lose the `id` column. Fix: read as `utf-8-sig`.\n6. **Permission blocks:** a scheduled task and global tool setup were refused as persistence/self-modification. Fix: you run those commands yourself with `!`."}
	],
